  "body": "Fixes #1669\n\n## Summary\n\n* **What is the goal of this PR?**\n  Add the transparent sleep-screen mode requested in #1669, refreshed for the current `develop` branch.\n* **What changes are included?**\n  * Adds a **Transparent** sleep-screen option and documents `/sleep-overlay.bmp`, `/.sleep-overlay/*.bmp`, and `/sleep-overlay/*.bmp`.\n  * Streams 32-bit BGRA overlays one row at a time so transparent pixels preserve the current page and opaque white pixels can erase it.\n  * Accepts regular BMPs through the existing `Bitmap::parseHeaders()` / `drawBitmap()` path, where white pixels preserve the existing framebuffer.\n  * Keeps a separate fixed-size recent-image history so Transparent and Custom rotation do not affect each other.\n  * Adds the new label in English, Spanish, Catalan, and Valencian.\n\n\n\n## Scope Check\n\nCrossPoint is intentionally narrow. See [SCOPE.md](../blob/master/SCOPE.md) and [ROADMAP.md](../blob/master/ROADMAP.md).\nPlease confirm:\n\n- [x] I have read SCOPE.md and ROADMAP.md.\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new built-in theme (themes are temporarily closed pending the move to SD-loaded themes).\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new external network connector (sync engine, cloud storage, remote file access, etc.).\n- [x] This PR is **not** an interactive app, writing tool, RSS/news/browser, media playback, or PDF feature.\n- [x] The stock firmware does not already handle this well, **and** no other popular CrossPoint fork already does\n      (or, if one does, I explain why CrossPoint still needs it below).\n- [x] If this PR touches `freeink-sdk/`, `lib/hal/`, the bootloader, OTA, or recovery code, I have coordinated with\n      the relevant maintainer.\n\n**If this PR was opened against the previous (broader) scope and was already in flight under Phase 0, link the\nrelevant Discussion or issue so reviewers can see the history.**\n\nThis refreshes #1994 after [Uri invited a fresh PR](https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader/pull/1994#issuecomment-5232084980). The core port remains authored by Pablo Cabeza, and the regular-BMP follow-up from [pblocz/crosspoint-reader#1](https://github.com/pblocz/crosspoint-reader/pull/1) remains separately attributed. Xteink's stock firmware has a comparable mode, but current CrossPoint does not; #1669 requests that parity.\n\n## Additional Context\n\n* The alpha path makes one checked `width * 4` allocation and reuses it for all rows and passes. The existing dimension cap bounds it at 8,192 bytes; it is released before any regular-BMP fallback.\n* Persistent state grows by 34 bytes: `uint16_t[16]` plus two `uint8_t` counters. Regular BMPs reuse the existing renderer path.\n* No `freeink-sdk/`, HAL, bootloader, OTA, or recovery files are changed.\n* Validation:\n  * `pio run -e default`\n  * `pio run -e simulator`\n  * `pio run -e simulator_x3`\n  * Automated X4 and X3 emulator runs for both regular and alpha BMP fixtures, with before/after screenshots and pixel-diff checks\n  * `git diff --check`\n* Emulator testing confirms transparent regions retain existing page content, opaque white erases it, and regular BMPs use the expected white-as-transparent behavior. This is emulator-only evidence; no physical X3/X4 validation was performed.\n\n---\n\n### AI Usage\n\nWhile CrossPoint doesn't have restrictions on AI tools in contributing, please be transparent about their usage as it\nhelps set the right context for reviewers.\n\nDid you use AI tools to help write this code? _**YES**_",
